WEBVTT

1
00:00:13.400 --> 00:00:15.382
Oliver's shouts, Harry Maylie and Mr.

2
00:00:15.402 --> 00:00:16.683
Giles rushed outside.

3
00:00:17.623 --> 00:00:21.687
They found Oliver, pale and agitated, pointing toward the meadows behind the house.

4
00:00:21.707 --> 00:00:24.389
"Fagin! Fagin!"

5
00:00:24.769 --> 00:00:25.390
cried Oliver.

6
00:00:26.330 --> 00:00:28.432
Mr. Giles had no idea what this name meant.

7
00:00:29.373 --> 00:00:32.996
But Harry had heard Oliver's story from his mother, so he knew who Fagin was.

8
00:00:34.112 --> 00:00:34.812
"Where did he go?"

9
00:00:35.793 --> 00:00:37.073
Harry picked up a large stick.

10
00:00:37.093 --> 00:00:41.475
"There!" Oliver pointed in the direction that Fagin had taken.

11
00:00:41.495 --> 00:00:43.616
"Then he must be in the ditch!

12
00:00:44.657 --> 00:00:45.157
Follow me!"

13
00:00:46.117 --> 00:00:47.778
Harry sprang over a hedge, with Mr.

14
00:00:47.798 --> 00:00:49.699
Giles and Oliver trying to keep up with him.

15
00:00:50.700 --> 00:00:53.841
Dr. Losberne, who was just returning from a walk, joined the chase.

16
00:00:55.102 --> 00:00:57.703
At last they reached the ditch, but no one was hiding in it.

17
00:00:58.763 --> 00:01:00.264
They walked to the top of a little hill.

18
00:01:01.364 --> 00:01:04.626
From there they could see all the open fields for several miles around.

19
00:01:06.348 --> 00:01:08.729
The village lay in one direction and the woods in another.

20
00:01:09.730 --> 00:01:12.592
But Fagin could not have reached either place without their spotting him.

21
00:01:12.612 --> 00:01:15.814
"It must have been a dream, Oliver," said Harry.

22
00:01:15.834 --> 00:01:17.916
"Oh no, sir."

23
00:01:19.056 --> 00:01:21.058
Oliver shuddered at the memory of Fagin's face.

24
00:01:21.078 --> 00:01:23.760
"I saw him too plainly for that.

25
00:01:24.840 --> 00:01:27.162
I saw them both as plainly as I see you now."

26
00:01:28.243 --> 00:01:29.243
"Both?" said Dr.

27
00:01:30.732 --> 00:01:31.913
Losberne. "Who was the other person?"

28
00:01:32.253 --> 00:01:32.793
asked Harry.

29
00:01:32.813 --> 00:01:36.335
"A strange man who shouted at me the day I took Mrs.

30
00:01:36.375 --> 00:01:37.476
Maylie's letter to the inn."

31
00:01:37.496 --> 00:01:39.877
"Are you sure they went this way?"

32
00:01:40.177 --> 00:01:40.817
Harry demanded.

33
00:01:41.958 --> 00:01:44.279
Oliver insisted, and the others wanted to believe him.

34
00:01:45.300 --> 00:01:47.981
But there were no footprints or any other sign of the two men.

35
00:01:49.742 --> 00:01:50.503
Harry sent Mr.

36
00:01:50.523 --> 00:01:52.484
Giles to ask about the two men at the village.

37
00:01:53.564 --> 00:01:54.425
No one had seen them.

38
00:01:55.485 --> 00:01:59.227
The next day Oliver and Harry went to the inn at the market town, hoping to hear something

39
00:01:59.267 --> 00:02:00.008
about the men there.

40
00:02:01.120 --> 00:02:05.783
This effort was equally fruitless, and in a few days, everyone forgot about the whole affair.

41
00:02:06.924 --> 00:02:08.605
Meanwhile Rose continued to recover.

42
00:02:09.685 --> 00:02:11.746
She left her room and was able to go outdoors.

43
00:02:12.887 --> 00:02:16.269
Cheerful voices and merry laughter could once again be heard in the cottage.

44
00:02:17.350 --> 00:02:20.031
But Oliver could not help noticing that something was wrong.

45
00:02:21.072 --> 00:02:24.194
Mrs. Maylie and her son were often closeted together for a long time.

46
00:02:25.235 --> 00:02:27.336
More than once Rose appeared to have been crying.

47
00:02:28.412 --> 00:02:32.634
At last one morning when Rose was alone in the breakfast room, Harry begged permission to speak to

48
00:02:32.694 --> 00:02:35.355
her. Rose turned pale and nodded.

49
00:02:35.375 --> 00:02:38.857
"I was brought here by the fear of losing you."

50
00:02:39.857 --> 00:02:40.838
He grasped her hand.

51
00:02:40.858 --> 00:02:45.120
"I dreaded that you would die and never know how devotedly I loved you."

52
00:02:46.120 --> 00:02:47.501
Tears came to Rose's eyes.

53
00:02:47.521 --> 00:02:49.642
"My own dear Rose!"

54
00:02:50.683 --> 00:02:51.403
Harry went on.

55
00:02:51.423 --> 00:02:53.524
"For years I've loved you.

56
00:02:54.632 --> 00:02:57.534
I hoped to win my way to fame and then come home and tell you I'd done it

57
00:02:57.614 --> 00:02:58.235
only for you.

58
00:02:59.315 --> 00:03:00.836
Alas, I am not famous.

59
00:03:01.877 --> 00:03:04.238
But I offer you my heart, which you have long possessed.

60
00:03:05.239 --> 00:03:06.080
Will you marry me?"

61
00:03:07.080 --> 00:03:08.461
"You have been ever so kind."

62
00:03:09.522 --> 00:03:11.063
Rose struggled to hold back her tears.

63
00:03:11.083 --> 00:03:14.365
"But I can only be your friend and not your wife."

64
00:03:15.426 --> 00:03:16.967
Harry still held Rose's hand.

65
00:03:18.068 --> 00:03:20.189
She covered her face with her other hand and wept.

66
00:03:20.209 --> 00:03:22.931
"And what are your reasons for this decision?"

67
00:03:23.251 --> 00:03:24.312
he asked in a low voice.

68
00:03:25.432 --> 00:03:27.674
"There is a stain upon my name," she said.

69
00:03:27.694 --> 00:03:33.358
"I cannot bring disgrace to you or to your mother, who has been like a mother to me.

70
00:03:34.539 --> 00:03:38.381
I won't have people saying that I married you to enhance my name and raise my position in

71
00:03:38.401 --> 00:03:38.802
the world."

72
00:03:38.822 --> 00:03:42.304
"If I'd been poor or sick, would you have turned me down?"

73
00:03:42.685 --> 00:03:43.205
asked Harry.

74
00:03:44.246 --> 00:03:47.688
Rose did not want to answer this question, but Harry pressed her to reply.

75
00:03:47.708 --> 00:03:52.231
"If you'd been even a little above me and I could have helped you, then we could have

76
00:03:52.251 --> 00:03:52.752
been happy.

77
00:03:53.676 --> 00:03:57.318
But now I'd only ruin your chances among ambitious and distinguished people.

78
00:03:58.478 --> 00:03:59.358
Farewell, Harry."

79
00:04:00.399 --> 00:04:01.879
Rose withdrew her hand from his.

80
00:04:01.899 --> 00:04:03.660
"Oh, Rose!"

81
00:04:04.020 --> 00:04:04.621
Harry cried.

82
00:04:04.641 --> 00:04:06.681
"Promise me one thing.

83
00:04:07.802 --> 00:04:10.163
Permit me to speak to you again on this subject in a year.

84
00:04:11.283 --> 00:04:12.704
And then I will never mention it again."

85
00:04:12.724 --> 00:04:18.966
"I'll promise you that," Rose said sadly, "although it will be useless to try to persuade me to

86
00:04:19.006 --> 00:04:19.507
marry you."

87
00:04:21.227 --> 00:04:25.433
She held out her hand again, but Harry embraced her instead and then hurried from the room.

88
00:04:26.514 --> 00:04:28.454
The next day Harry joined Oliver and Dr.

89
00:04:28.474 --> 00:04:29.715
Losberne at the breakfast table.

90
00:04:29.735 --> 00:04:34.057
"So you're going to be my traveling companion today," the doctor said to Harry.

91
00:04:35.117 --> 00:04:38.098
"Yesterday you were going to stay here and accompany your mother to the seaside.

92
00:04:39.159 --> 00:04:43.381
Then last night you urged, with great mystery, that we start out this morning before the ladies arise.

93
00:04:44.521 --> 00:04:45.341
What's going on?"

94
00:04:45.361 --> 00:04:47.702
"I simply changed my mind."

95
00:04:48.763 --> 00:04:49.843
Harry studied his tea.

96
00:04:49.863 --> 00:04:55.233
"Why? Have you heard something from those who have been encouraging you to run for Parliament?"

97
00:04:56.374 --> 00:04:59.655
"No. It's unlikely I'd hear anything at this time of year."

98
00:04:59.675 --> 00:05:03.016
"Well, you're an odd fellow," said the doctor.

99
00:05:03.036 --> 00:05:08.158
"But I know there are people working to get you into Parliament in the election before Christmas."

100
00:05:08.178 --> 00:05:12.380
"We shall see," Harry mumbled, not wanting to say anything more.

101
00:05:13.481 --> 00:05:14.721
The coach pulled up to the door.

102
00:05:15.842 --> 00:05:19.603
Mr. Giles came in for the baggage, and the doctor bustled out to see that it was loaded

103
00:05:19.663 --> 00:05:23.009
properly. "Oliver," said Harry in a low voice.

104
00:05:24.150 --> 00:05:25.011
"You can write well now?"

105
00:05:26.192 --> 00:05:27.513
Oliver looked up in surprise.

106
00:05:27.533 --> 00:05:29.234
"Yes, sir."

107
00:05:29.254 --> 00:05:31.896
"I won't be home again for some time.

108
00:05:33.037 --> 00:05:34.699
I wish you'd write to me every other week.

109
00:05:35.699 --> 00:05:36.320
Will you do that?"

110
00:05:36.340 --> 00:05:38.442
"Oh certainly, sir.

111
00:05:39.583 --> 00:05:40.583
I'll be proud to do it."

112
00:05:40.603 --> 00:05:43.566
"I'd like to know how my mother and Miss Rose are.

113
00:05:44.627 --> 00:05:47.169
You can tell me about the walks you take and what you talk about.

114
00:05:48.330 --> 00:05:50.992
And whether she—I mean they—seem happy and well.

115
00:05:51.992 --> 00:05:52.713
Do you understand?"

116
00:05:52.733 --> 00:05:56.075
"Oh yes," replied Oliver.

117
00:05:56.095 --> 00:06:01.278
"I'd rather you didn't mention this to the ladies because it might upset my mother," Harry said hurriedly.

118
00:06:01.298 --> 00:06:03.620
"Remember to tell me everything.

119
00:06:04.721 --> 00:06:05.581
I'm depending on you."

120
00:06:06.742 --> 00:06:08.944
Oliver was pleased and honored by his request.

121
00:06:10.064 --> 00:06:11.505
Harry went outside to join Dr.

122
00:06:11.545 --> 00:06:16.829
Losberne. As Harry jumped into the coach, he cast a last glance up at one of the cottage

123
00:06:16.869 --> 00:06:21.212
windows. Jingling and clattering, the coach pulled away in a cloud of dust.

124
00:06:22.316 --> 00:06:26.158
But there was one person whose eyes remained fixed on the spot where the coach had disappeared.

125
00:06:26.178 --> 00:06:31.541
"Harry seems happy," Rose said to herself as she sat at the upstairs window.

126
00:06:31.561 --> 00:06:33.582
"I'm very glad of that."

127
00:06:34.563 --> 00:06:36.044
But tears ran down her face.
